# Large generated artifacts that aren't reproducible from git state alone:
# - Corpus JSONL is regeneratable from the labeler binary + ripgrep clone
# - Facts JSONL and per-commit diffs are regeneratable from the labeler's
#   `emit-facts` / `emit-diffs` subcommands over the corpus + ripgrep clone
# - Spot-check working-copy files (.bak, .PARKED) are local-only
# - phase1.sqlite is a working store rebuildable from the same inputs as
#   predictions.jsonl / rule_traces.jsonl; pilot precedent does not commit it
corpus/*.jsonl
facts/*.facts.jsonl
facts/*.diffs/
spotcheck/*.bak
spotcheck/*.PARKED
work/
results/**/phase1/phase1.sqlite
results/**/phase1/phase1.sqlite-shm
results/**/phase1/phase1.sqlite-wal
results/**/phase1-v1.4/phase1.sqlite
results/**/phase1-v1.4/phase1.sqlite-shm
results/**/phase1-v1.4/phase1.sqlite-wal

# Full-corpus sidecar artifacts (Plan A.2 flask v1.3, 2026-05-19) — too large
# to track; regeneratable from labeler at bf56f40 + phase1 over the corpus.
# Baseline is synthetic (placeholder for phase1's --baseline-run loader);
# its manifest.json/metrics.json are stub files, not real LLM artifacts.
results/flask-heldout-2026-05-19-fullcorpus/phase1/predictions.jsonl
results/flask-heldout-2026-05-19-fullcorpus/phase1/rule_traces.jsonl
results/flask-heldout-2026-05-19-fullcorpus/baseline/predictions.jsonl
results/flask-heldout-2026-05-19-fullcorpus/baseline/manifest.json
results/flask-heldout-2026-05-19-fullcorpus/baseline/metrics.json

# Keep the directory itself tracked via .gitkeep
!.gitkeep
